    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **governance.test.js** - Missing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` export\n**Problem:** The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Solution:** Added named exports in `src/finetune/index.js` for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\n### 2. **eval/index.test.js** - Incorrect toxicity scoring\n**Problem:** The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving references as the second parameter and treating them as banned terms, causing safe outputs like `'Hello'` and `'friendly world'` to be incorrectly flagged as toxic.\n\n**Solution:** Removed the `bannedTerms` parameter from `toxicityMetric` in `src/eval/metrics.js` so it only accepts outputs and always uses the default banned terms list.\n\n**Test Results:** \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files",
